# Internal names that are matched as whole tokens, not substrings, because
# each is also part of ordinary words (or is a host or a repository path). Kept
# as digests so this file does not name them either. One per line: the name's
# length in characters, then the SHA-256 of the name in lowercase.
# scripts/check-no-internal-names.sh reads it (the lint job in CI) and says
# what counts as a whole token.
#
# To add a name:  printf %s 'name' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]' | shasum -a 256
# and prepend its length.
